{"title":"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Sarah intended to multiply a two-digit number and a three-digit number, but she left out the multiplication sign and simply placed the two-digit number to the left of the three-digit number, thereby forming a five-digit number.  This number is exactly nine times the product Sarah should have obtained.  What is the sum of the two-digit number and the three-digit number?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the two-digit number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the three-digit number. Putting together the given, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/2/7b2f2769e97fa67ca21e36968f042a6c51715386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000x+y=9xy \\Longrightarrow 9xy-1000x-y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"334\" height=\"16\" />. Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simon%27s_Favorite_Factoring_Trick\" title=\"Simon&#39;s Favorite Factoring Trick\">SFFT</a>, this factorizes to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae970537ab729709a1a71f44ed672671ed46f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9x-1)\\left(y-\\dfrac{1000}{9}\\right)=\\dfrac{1000}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"229\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d434f5fe7e6f32dcc3a7fa80c431b9b0697fb0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9x-1)(9y-1000)=1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c2d4e6036f5538b53acb43f85cb1fff5177bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89 &lt; 9x-1 &lt; 890$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"144\" height=\"13\" />, we can use trial and error on factors of 1000. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2bc51386589af406cab2b904b1e516be61bbb78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9x - 1 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />, we get a non-integer. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b8489fc36c910b460247af4eede30083df084dd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9x - 1 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1f563320251baffd8c317c10f81a836df20c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45b536a552412ee968662df98936eaecece0e3cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=112$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, which satisifies the conditions. Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265e6b754156340c092602efc0c5bcebf654e73f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$112 + 14 = \\boxed{126}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As shown above, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6847e8f52a67b898dec47eabb978a6c308950b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000x+y=9xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855755c275b9ac16d41cc595901363604a8b8540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000/y=9-1/x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b321bb70bd52635192178b548af753f66a1ba4a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000/y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> must be just a little bit smaller than 9, so we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45b536a552412ee968662df98936eaecece0e3cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=112$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1f563320251baffd8c317c10f81a836df20c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, and the solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/7/26700f6a87398112e9dee5442a47483da2e37194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{126}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To begin, we rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/89364a9e736df4a335f51059a22cb1093cf6f86e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10a+b)*(100x+10y+z)*9 = 10000a + 1000b + 100x + 10y + z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"535\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>as\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8af15f90d1fc96e33d56a683936ea9e990221c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(90a+9b-1)(100x+10y+z) = 10000a + 1000b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"391\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5c94aed07038614456ba3a649077bedc81f814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(90a+9b-1)(100x+10y+z) = 1000(10a + b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"377\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThis is the most important part: Notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a2cecf68b8cf9c7ed3da3c3f64294ae20113d4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(90a+9b-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a756ae5b246a6eddcf102e65ddba41ceada1da2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 \\pmod{10a+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735f2d97b67a30871416b2d028f23733af92ca05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000(10a + b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c07a7accad82e0c594565cb0543106e3b71841f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\pmod{10a+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8e9826584b2e0d1de535fd029711139d6ffcf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(100x+10y+z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/140d2c98dd46498ecfc671e7402785819423dfcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\pmod{10+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />. Rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8e9826584b2e0d1de535fd029711139d6ffcf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(100x+10y+z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b523aac5b7f19430c24076aaec7d5ed357b30d26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times(10a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a187bfa044458e3e06cd911620c93364f7ed95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(90a+9b-1)\\times n(10a+b)= 1000(10a + b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"352\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/b/51b45e6ccc86a96224386524245286e6a0fbfd44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(90a+9b-1)\\times n= 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNow we have to find a number that divides 1000 using prime factors 2 or 5 and is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1ccd90d6e251ab35d471382ebc16c8d67188cdce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\pmod9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />. It is quick to find there is only one: 125. That gives 14 as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8b0d985d7137b67edcdd55029a03843223fe5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> and 112 as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f77ed56a012da687f53d23bb3003ff99c21121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100x+10y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265e6b754156340c092602efc0c5bcebf654e73f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$112 + 14 = \\boxed{126}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>-jackshi2006\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME\" title=\"1997 AIME\">1997 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1997 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190318\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 250/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6383/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.769      1 -total\n 58.17%    8.009      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.50%    5.439      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3005:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190318 and revision id 159596. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}